## 1. Navigation & Files

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `pwd` | Print current directory (where am I?) |
| `ls` | List files in current directory |
| `ls -la` | List **all** files (incl. hidden), long format (permissions, owner, size, date) |
| `ls -lh` | Long format, human-readable sizes (KB/MB/GB) |
| `cd foldername` | Move into a folder |
| `cd ..` | Move up one directory |
| `cd ~` or `cd` | Go to home directory |
| `cd -` | Go back to previous directory |
| `mkdir foldername` | Make a new directory |
| `mkdir -p a/b/c` | Make nested directories in one shot |
| `touch file.txt` | Create an empty file (or update its timestamp) |
| `cp file1 file2` | Copy file1 to file2 |
| `cp -r dir1 dir2` | Copy a directory recursively |
| `mv file1 file2` | Move or rename a file |
| `rm file.txt` | Delete a file |
| `rm -r foldername` | Delete a folder and its contents (careful!) |
| `rm -rf foldername` | Force delete, no prompts (**very careful**) |
| `find / -name "file.txt"` | Search the whole filesystem for a file by name |
| `find . -type f -mtime -1` | Find files modified in the last 1 day (forensics-useful) |
| `locate filename` | Fast file search using an index (needs `updatedb`) |
| `tree` | Show directory structure as a tree (may need install) |

