## 2. Viewing & Editing Files

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `cat file.txt` | Print entire file to screen |
| `less file.txt` | View file page-by-page (`q` to quit, `/word` to search) |
| `head file.txt` | Show first 10 lines |
| `head -n 50 file.txt` | Show first 50 lines |
| `tail file.txt` | Show last 10 lines |
| `tail -f /var/log/auth.log` | **Live-follow** a file as it grows (great for watching logs) |
| `nano file.txt` | Beginner-friendly terminal text editor |
| `vim file.txt` | Powerful but steeper-learning-curve editor |
| `wc -l file.txt` | Count lines in a file |
| `diff file1 file2` | Show differences between two files |

