## 4. Permissions & Ownership (core security concept)

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ls -l` | Shows permissions like `-rwxr-xr--` |
| `chmod 755 file.sh` | Set permissions (owner: rwx, group: r-x, other: r-x) |
| `chmod +x script.sh` | Make a file executable |
| `chown user:group file.txt` | Change file owner/group |
| `sudo command` | Run a command as superuser/root |
| `whoami` | Show current logged-in user |
| `id` | Show your user ID, group ID, and group memberships |
| `su username` | Switch to another user |

**Permission string cheat:** `r`=read(4), `w`=write(2), `x`=execute(1). `rwxr-xr--` = owner has all 3, group has read+execute, others have read only.

