## 9. Redirection & Pipes (glue that makes Linux powerful)

| Symbol | What it does |
|---|---|
| `\|` | Pipe — send output of one command into another |
| `>` | Redirect output to a file (overwrite) |
| `>>` | Redirect output to a file (append) |
| `<` | Take input from a file |
| `&&` | Run second command only if first succeeds |
| `;` | Run commands sequentially regardless of success |
| `2>&1` | Redirect error output along with standard output |

**Example combo:** `grep "failed" auth.log | awk '{print $9}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr`
→ finds failed logins, pulls out the IP/user field, and ranks by frequency. This exact pattern shows up constantly in log analysis.

